-- title:
--   Vertical twist to multidegree zero fixing the generic fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a package $\mathfrak X$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data over $\mathbb Z$ (`DRModelPackage p`), a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ with a ring map $O \to \kappa$, and a resolved model package $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ over these data, with structure morphism $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ (written `𝔛reg.toBase`) and special-fibre components `𝔛reg.comp v` indexed by $v \in$ `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_{x} \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(x)-1)$, each an ideal sheaf datum on $Y$. Let $m \in \mathbb N$, let $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_{m-1}$ be sections of `𝔛reg.toBase` (morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ composing with it to the identity), let $\mathrm{pos},\mathrm{neg} : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb N$ and $v : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ components. Assume that for each $j$ the specialisation $\sigma_j(\text{closed point of } O)$ lies in `𝔛reg.smoothOffEdges`, lies in the support of `𝔛reg.comp (v j)`, and lies in the support of no other component; that $\sum_j (\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j) = 0$; and that the vector $c = \sum_j \delta_{v_j}(\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j)$ lies in the image of the additive map $\alpha(a)_j = \sum_i a_i \cdot t.\mathrm{inter}(i,j)$ attached to the table `x0MqResolvedTable 𝔛reg.width`, whose multiplicities are all $1$ and whose intersection numbers are the adjacency numbers $x0MqAdj$ off the diagonal, with the negative of the row sum on the diagonal. Then there exist $a^{+}, a^{-} : \text{components} \to \mathbb N$ such that: (i) for every component $c_0$ one has $\bigl(\sum_j \delta_{v_j}(\mathrm{pos}_j-\mathrm{neg}_j)\bigr)(c_0) + \alpha\bigl(a^{+}-a^{-}\bigr)(c_0) = 0$; (ii) the module on $Y$ obtained as the iterated tensor product, over $j$ in `List.finRange m`, of $(\sigma_j^{*}\text{-kernel})^{\mathrm{pos}_j}$-dual-module and $(\sigma_j^{*}\text{-kernel})^{\mathrm{neg}_j}$-module, with base term $\bigl(\prod_F (\text{comp } F)^{a^{+}_F}\bigr)^{\vee}\text{-module} \otimes \bigl(\prod_F (\text{comp } F)^{a^{-}_F}\bigr)\text{-module}$, is invertible in the sense that every point has a neighbourhood on which it pulls back to the structure sheaf; and (iii) its pullback along $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ for the base change $\operatorname{Spec}\mathrm{Frac}(O) \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ admits an isomorphism to the corresponding fold over the generic fibre, built from the section twists `sectionTwist 𝔛reg.toBase (σ j) _ (pos j)`, that is the dual of the $\mathrm{pos}_j$-th power of the ideal `sectionIdeal`, tensored with the module of the $\mathrm{neg}_j$-th power of that ideal, ending at the tensor unit.
--
--   This is the vertical-correction step for divisor classes on a resolved Deligne–Rapoport model: an invertible sheaf supported by horizontal sections of prescribed multiplicities is adjusted by a combination of components of the special fibre so as to have degree zero on every component, without altering its generic fibre. It is used in the construction of sections of the relative Picard functor over $O$ from degree-zero divisor classes on the generic fibre.
